[2026-09-07T12:30:00Z] [CHALLENGER] completed F2-T2 -> /src/db_challenger.py. Independent DatabaseManager variant implemented from spec §10 only (src/db.py NOT read — does not exist yet). Structural differences from the spec reference implementation (which F2-T1 executor is expected to follow closely):
  (1) Composition over monolith: DatabaseManager delegates to _WriteGate (owns RW conn + RLock) and _ReadPool (bounded pool of read cursors) — vs reference's single class with _read_only_conn() helper.
  (2) threading.RLock (reentrant) vs threading.Lock — write methods can compose without deadlock.
  (3) Bounded cursor pool (cursors derived from the RW instance via cursor()) vs per-query read-only connections. NECESSARY DEVIATION: DuckDB 1.4.3 on Windows rejects opening a read_only=True connection to a file that already has an open RW connection ("Can't open a connection to same database file with a different configuration than existing connections"). The reference's _read_only_conn() approach would fail on this DuckDB version; the executor (F2-T1) will hit the same wall. Verified concurrent cursor reads (6 threads x 50 queries) succeed with no errors.
  (4) Read-only enforcement at the SQL layer: execute_query validates the statement begins with SELECT or WITH (case-insensitive) before reaching DuckDB — defense-in-depth, same principle as the Flight server's _validate_select_only. Rejects DELETE/INSERT/DROP/etc with ValueError. Observable-equivalent to the reference's read-only connection rejection.
  (5) INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (Date, Ticker) DO UPDATE SET ... vs MERGE INTO ... WHEN MATCHED/NOT MATCHED. Same upsert semantics against PRIMARY KEY (Date, Ticker).
  (6) Named SQL parameters ($ticker, $split_date, $factor, $target_date, $version) vs positional ? placeholders.
  (7) Context-manager protocol (__enter__/__exit__) + __del__ safety net vs no context-manager support.
  (8) Upsert stages via pa.Table.from_pandas(df, preserve_index=False) instead of conn.register(df) directly — pandas 3.0.5's new str dtype is NOT recognized by DuckDB's pandas registration path ("Data type 'str' not implemented"); Arrow staging sidesteps this.
  (9) execute_query normalizes DuckDB 1.4's RecordBatchReader (returned by .arrow()) to pa.Table via .read_all() for cross-version compatibility; the reference's .arrow() return would be a RecordBatchReader on this version, not pa.Table.
Same public API as spec §10: DatabaseManager(db_path), _init_schema, execute_query->pa.Table, upsert_dataframe->int, purge_ticker, is_split_processed, record_split, delete_ticker_data, get_existing_tickers, get_aligned_start_date, detect_new_tickers, generate_top_20_dollar_volume, close (CHECKPOINT). Schema identical: daily_quotes (Volume DOUBLE, PK Date+Ticker), splits_processed (PK Ticker+SplitDate), schema_version.
